the lowest fixed cost. The risks: a 4-day batch of item 0 exactly matches its 4-day shelf life, so leftovers are written off, and deliveries of about 187 units nearly fill the 188-unit warehouse, so any carry-over is lost on arrival.\n- **Candidate 4** orders about 1.15× for item 0 and 1.25× for item 1. The day-11 delivery (99 + 89) is exactly 188, so any leftover stock overflows, and surplus item 1 builds up until it spoils.\n- **Candidate 1** orders about 0.9× for item 0, and item 0 loses 9 per unit short. Item 1 is near 1.0×, which still falls short of the higher average demand.\n- **Candidate 2** has well-sized orders but 171 more in fixed cost than the 3-day plans.\n- **Candidate 7** pays the same fixed cost as 2 but holds item 1 in larger 4-day batches, so it should come out slightly worse.\n\nOverall ranking: 5 ≈ 3 > 0 > 4 ≈ 2 > 7 > 1 > 6. The middle (0, 4, 2, 7, 1) is close, so those probabilities stay near 0.5."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5054, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5054}, "output_tokens": 10, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:25:54.364Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWD4Cz1DrEUN2dWws8z1"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RAsYGb7qp6cyaVPTqkm6SN", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWD4DFseQXykUBJKtXm1", "type": "message", "role": "assist